_margin": 0.75, "sigma_race": 5.0, "sigma_total": 5.82, "baseline_margin": 2.52, "analyst_adjustment": -0.02, "key_factors": ["Talarico leads recent polls by roughly 3 points on average, including high-quality surveys from NYT/Siena, Marist and YouGov", "Paxton is weighed down by heavy outside opposition spending ($27M against him) and a divisive primary win over Cornyn", "Talarico's record $64M fundraising and $21.5M cash advantage fuel a strong advertising presence", "Texas's Republican-leaning fundamentals (PVI R+6) cap Democratic upside in a neutral environment"], "rationale": "The polling average puts Talarico up about 3 points, prediction markets price him near 62-64%, and most expert raters call it a Tossup with a few moving to Lean D. The state's Republican lean and Paxton's ability to consolidate the GOP base keep this short of Likely D, but the weight of polling, money and market pricing justifies a modest Democratic edge.", "watch": "Whether Talarico's narrow polling slippage continues through early voting, or controversies like the 'God is nonbinary' remark and town hall scrutiny erode his standing further.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Open seat: John Cornyn (R) is not on the ballot."]}, "overview": "Texas's open Senate seat has become one of the cycle's marquee contests. With John Cornyn denied renomination, Democrat James Talarico faces scandal-plagued Attorney General Ken Paxton. Recent polls from mid-October consistently show Talarico ahead by two to six points, though his lead has narrowed as early voting nears. Prediction markets give him roughly a two-in-three chance, and most expert raters call the race a Tossup, with a couple moving to Lean D.\n\nTalarico holds a decisive financial edge, having raised a record $68.6 million against Paxton's $9.2 million, and outside groups have poured more than $27 million into attacks on Paxton. Still, Texas's Republican-leaning electorate keeps the race competitive, and Paxton retains a loyal conservative base. The race sits as a modest but genuine Democratic edge heading into the final weeks.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.6697, "margin": 2.08}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.6924, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7255, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.6997, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.6523, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.6444, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.6983, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.7151, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-09-30", "p_dem": 0.701, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-01", "p_dem": 0.7008, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-02", "p_dem": 0.6832, "margin": 2.2}, {"date": "2026-10-03", "p_dem": 0.7125, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-04", "p_dem": 0.7022, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-05", "p_dem": 0.6597, "margin": 2.6}, {"date": "2026-10-06", "p_dem": 0.6724, "margin": 2.8}, {"date": "2026-10-07", "p_dem": 0.6815, "margin": 3.0}, {"date": "2026-10-08", "p_dem": 0.6849, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-09", "p_dem": 0.6371, "margin": 2.3}, {"date": "2026-10-10", "p_dem": 0.6509, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-11", "p_dem": 0.6562, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-12", "p_dem": 0.7133, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-13", "p_dem": 0.6818, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-14", "p_dem": 0.6846, "margin": 2.5}, {"date": "2026-10-15", "p_dem": 0.6501, "margin": 2.5}]}